Capacity [text box] - Converter
Type the Capacity into the text box, i.e., the number of MUs, which the Converter can hold at any one
time.
Remarks
The default value -1 stands for an infinite capacity.
If the Converter conveys MUs along the insertion direction, you can, for example, use the Capacity to
allow the Converter to only convey this number of MUs at the same time.
This only limits the possible number of MUs. If the Converter conveys MUs it still conveys a single MU at a
time though.
