Relative Converting Point For Length
Type the relative position of the converting point along the length of the Converter into the text box.
Remarks
The converting point is the point at which the Converter changes the conveying direction of the MUs it
conveys.
You can type in a value between 0.0 and 1.0, denoting a position between 0 % and 100 %.
Note
The Converter does not show the location of the converting point on its graphic in the Frame.
