Strategy [drop-down list] - Converter
Select the Strategy according to which the Converter conveys the MUs to the next material flow object.
Remarks
You can select one of these settings:
• Default Exit
Makes all MUs exit through the Default Exit which you select to the successor attached to that exit.
• Straight
Conveys the MU straight through to the next station.
If several equally fast routes exist, the route, which leads straight through the Converter will be
preferred, as the parts do not have to be singularized for this. If several Converters are located within
the fastest route, Plant Simulation selects the route of the equally fast routes where the part must be
converted the least. A useful side effect is that Plant Simulation finds the clearly shortest route more
often, meaning that the entire route to the destination is known immediately.
• MU Attribute
Conveys the MUs according to a built-in or a user-defined attribute of the MU. Click Open List and enter
the name of the Attribute of the MU, the Value of the attribute, and select on which Side it is to exit.
Type in the number of the Default Exit. Repeat this for each attribute you specify.
The numbers designate the side of the Converter at which the MU exits. The figures below illustrate the
sides depending on the direction in which you inserted the Converter into your simulation model.
• MU Name
Conveys the MU according to its Name. Click Open List and type in the name of the MU and select on
Which Side it is to exit.
Enter the number of the Default Exit.
Strategy [drop-down list] - Converter
11-2254 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Method
Conveys the MUs according to the attribute ExitForMU you enter into the Strategy Method. Here you
determine the side of the Converter at which the MU will exit the Converter. Select the method or enter
the name of the method into the text box Strategy Method.
• Feed in
Enables MUs from a branch line to only enter the main line if no MU is located on the main line within
the Free Space which you enter. The Free Space is the distance between two successive MUs on the
main line.
Note
The first-come-first-served principle applies for all strategies, except for Feed In, meaning a MU, which
has a matching entrance and a matching target, still cannot enter the object after the Moving Time
has passed if another MU is already waiting, even if a Moving Time is required for this part as
well. The main conveyor only has precedence for the strategy Feed In. Waiting MUs from a branch
conveyor still have to wait unless the Moving Time has already started.
• Method at Converting Point
Determines the target with the attribute ExitForMU at the converting point, not already before the MU
enters the Converter. This strategy is only available for a Capacity of 1.
Strategy [drop-down list] - Converter
Plant Simulation Help 11-2255
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The MU always stops at the converting point. Then, Plant Simulation calls the method for determining
the target. In the method you can, for example, use ?.ExitForMU := 1.
Select the method or type the name of the method into the text box Strategy Method.
Note
As the Strategy Method is used for determining the side of the exit, the Strategy Method will not be
called if the MU has a route and Automatic Routing is activated.
