Moving Time [drop-down list] - Converter
The Moving Time is the time it takes the Converter to lift the MU onto a different conveying level and to
then lower itself and move back to the default position.
Remarks
The Moving Time always elapses when the Converter has to change the direction of the MU and when a
MU enters from a side, i.e., not along the preferred insertion direction.
Select a distribution for the Moving Time from the drop-down list, and type the values, which that
distribution requires, into the text box.
Plant Simulation shows these values along the upper border of the tab. You can also type in a constant
time (Const).
If you select the Formula distribution, you can type in a numeric expression or the name of a Method. You
can use the anonymous identifier @ to access the part for which the Moving Time applies.
