Tab Costs
Select costs settings for the object on the Tab Costs.
While the Converter transports parts costs accrue which result from the sum of the total investment costs
and the total operating costs.
Note
The total investment costs only accrue during the Depreciation Period.
The costs are allocated to the part, proportional to the length of the part to the active length of the
Converter, as accrued costs. Thus, a longer part is allocated higher costs as it occupies a greater part of
the Converter.
If the Converter is empty, the costs remain with the Converter as general costs.
See also
Simulate the Accrued Costs of the Machines
CostAnalyzer > How the CostAnalyzer Assigns Costs to Part Types
